# Workboard

Requires Node.js 22.22.1. No external dependencies or installation are needed.

Run:

```sh
PORT=8080 DB_PATH=./data/workboard.sqlite npm start
```

Open `http://localhost:8080`. The server binds to `0.0.0.0`.
`PORT` defaults to `8080`; `DB_PATH` defaults to `data/workboard.sqlite`.
Use the same database path across restarts to retain projects, tasks, completion state,
archive state, renamed project names and task titles, task priorities, project task-priority defaults,
and task due dates. Existing databases are upgraded automatically.
`GET /health` returns `{"status":"ok"}`.

Verify:

```sh
npm test
```

Each project page supports task creation, completion checkboxes, and an All/Open/Completed
filter. A Priority filter offers All, Low, Normal, and High, initially All. Tasks must
match both filters and remain in creation order. Changing either filter or editing
a task keeps both selections; completion and priority edits immediately refresh the
matching rows. Both filters work in archived projects and leave summary counts unchanged.
New tasks are open, and both project names and task titles are trimmed.
The project list starts with Active projects and can show Archived projects. Archive
and restore preserve tasks; archived project pages allow viewing and filtering but
disable task creation and completion changes. Each project row summarizes completion
across all its tasks.

Active project pages provide New project name and Rename project controls. Renaming
trims the name and preserves the project's URL, creation order, tasks, and completion
summary. Blank names show an alert. Archived projects disable renaming until restored.

Each task row provides New task title and Rename task controls. Renaming trims the
title and preserves task identity, ownership, creation order, completion state, and
summary counts. Blank titles show an alert. Archived projects disable these controls
until restored.

Each task row has a Task priority combobox with Low, Normal, and High options.
Existing tasks default to Normal during migration. Priority changes persist independently
without affecting titles, completion, order, ownership, or summaries. Archived
projects disable priority editing until restored.

Each project page has a Default task priority combobox with Low, Normal, and High
options. Projects initially default to Normal; new tasks inherit the project's saved
default. Changing the default leaves existing tasks and both filter selections alone.
Defaults persist independently through reloads, restarts, renaming, and archive/restore.
Archived projects display their saved default with editing disabled until restored.

Each task row has a Task due date textbox and Save due date button. Dates start empty;
saving whitespace clears them. Nonempty values are trimmed and must be real Gregorian
dates in YYYY-MM-DD format, with years 0001 through 9999. Invalid dates show an alert
and preserve the saved date. Dates are stored as calendar-day text without timezone
conversion. Saving dates leaves task identity, other fields, filters, and summaries
unchanged. Archived projects disable both controls until restored.

Each project page provides Due from and Due through textboxes and Apply due range.
Applied boundaries are inclusive and intersect completion and priority filters.
Blank boundaries are unbounded; undated tasks match only when both are blank.
Invalid dates or reversed boundaries show an alert and retain the last applied range.
Task edits immediately refresh matching rows. Renames, creation, and default changes
retain all applied filters. Range controls work in archived projects, and reopening
a project starts with empty boundaries. Calendar validation is shared with due-date
saving so both use the same Gregorian rules without timezone conversions.

The integration test uses an isolated database, exercises project and task validation,
creation order, project isolation, and completion updates, and restarts the server to
verify persistence, database migration, archive/restore, and completion summaries.
The browser-code interaction test uses a small DOM harness to check task validation,
filtering, checkbox updates, save-error recovery, project archive/restore, summaries,
archived page controls, and renaming without external dependencies. Integration checks
also verify rename validation, identity preservation, archived restrictions, and
renamed names surviving server restarts. Priority checks cover migration of existing
tasks, defaults, independent edits, invalid values, save-error recovery, unchanged
completion summaries, and priority persistence through renaming, archive/restore,
filter changes, and server restarts.
Combined-filter checks cover every completion/priority combination, selection retention,
task edits leaving the matching list, rename membership, and archived filtering.
Project-default checks cover migration, independent defaults, future-task inheritance,
unchanged existing tasks and filters, save-error recovery, archived restrictions,
renaming, restoration, and restart persistence.
Due-date checks cover empty defaults and migration, leap years and calendar boundaries,
invalid-value rejection, trimming, clearing, independent values, unchanged task data
and summaries, retained filters, rename preservation, archived controls, and restart
persistence.
Due-range checks cover inclusive and one-sided boundaries, undated tasks, every
completion/priority combination, invalid calendar dates and reversed ranges,
unapplied text, edit-triggered membership changes, selection retention, archived
filtering, empty initial boundaries, and accessible controls.
import { test } from 'node:test';
import assert from 'node:assert/strict';
import { spawn } from 'node:child_process';
import { once } from 'node:events';
import { mkdir, mkdtemp, rm } from 'node:fs/promises';
import { resolve } from 'node:path';
import { DatabaseSync } from 'node:sqlite';

async function start(databasePath) {
  const child = spawn(process.execPath, ['server.js'], {
    env: { ...process.env, PORT: '0', DB_PATH: databasePath },
    stdio: ['ignore', 'pipe', 'pipe'],
  });
  let output = '';
  let errors = '';
  child.stderr.on('data', chunk => { errors += chunk; });
  const url = await new Promise((resolveUrl, reject) => {
    const timeout = setTimeout(() => {
      child.kill();
      reject(new Error(`Server startup timed out: ${errors}`));
    }, 10000);
    child.stdout.on('data', chunk => {
      output += chunk;
      const match = output.match(/listening on port (\d+)/);
      if (match) {
        clearTimeout(timeout);
        resolveUrl(`http://127.0.0.1:${match[1]}`);
      }
    });
    child.once('error', error => { clearTimeout(timeout); reject(error); });
    child.once('exit', code => {
      clearTimeout(timeout);
      reject(new Error(`Server exited (${code}): ${errors}`));
    });
  });
  return { url, async stop() {
    const exited = once(child, 'exit');
    child.kill('SIGTERM');
    await exited;
  } };
}

test('projects and tasks validate, stay isolated, and survive a restart', async () => {
  await mkdir('data', { recursive: true });
  const directory = await mkdtemp(resolve('data', 'test-'));
  const databasePath = resolve(directory, 'projects.sqlite');
  let server;
  try {
    // Upgrade a database with the schema used before archive support.
    const legacy = new DatabaseSync(databasePath);
    legacy.exec(`CREATE TABLE projects (
      position INTEGER PRIMARY KEY AUTOINCREMENT, id TEXT NOT NULL UNIQUE, name TEXT NOT NULL
    ); INSERT INTO projects (id, name) VALUES ('legacy', 'Existing project');
    CREATE TABLE tasks (
      position INTEGER PRIMARY KEY AUTOINCREMENT, id TEXT NOT NULL UNIQUE,
      project_id TEXT NOT NULL REFERENCES projects(id), title TEXT NOT NULL,
      completed INTEGER NOT NULL DEFAULT 0 CHECK (completed IN (0, 1))
    ); INSERT INTO tasks (id, project_id, title, completed)
      VALUES ('legacy-task', 'legacy', 'Existing task', 1)`);
    legacy.close();
    server = await start(databasePath);
    const get = async path => {
      const response = await fetch(server.url + path);
      assert.equal(response.status, 200);
      return response.json();
    };
    const create = name => fetch(server.url + '/api/projects', {
      method: 'POST',
      headers: { 'Content-Type': 'application/json' },
      body: JSON.stringify({ name }),
    });
    assert.deepEqual(await get('/health'), { status: 'ok' });
    const existing = { id: 'legacy', name: 'Existing project', archived: false, default_task_priority: 'Normal', total: 1, completed: 1 };
    assert.deepEqual(await get('/api/projects'), [existing]);
    const legacyTasks = [{ id: 'legacy-task', title: 'Existing task', completed: true, priority: 'Normal', due_date: '' }];
    assert.deepEqual(await get('/api/projects/legacy/tasks'), legacyTasks);
    for (const name of ['', ' \t\n ']) {
      const response = await create(name);
      assert.equal(response.status, 400);
      assert.deepEqual(await response.json(), { error: 'Project name is required' });
    }
    assert.deepEqual(await get('/api/projects'), [existing]);
    const firstResponse = await create('  First project  ');
    assert.equal(firstResponse.status, 201);
    const first = await firstResponse.json();
    assert.equal(first.name, 'First project');
    assert.ok(first.id);
    const secondResponse = await create('Second project');
    const second = await secondResponse.json();
    assert.notEqual(first.id, second.id);
    assert.deepEqual(await get('/api/projects'), [existing, first, second]);
    assert.equal(first.archived, false);
    assert.equal(first.total, 0);
    assert.equal(first.completed, 0);
    assert.deepEqual(await get(`/api/projects/${first.id}`), first);
    const firstTasks = `/api/projects/${first.id}/tasks`;
    const secondTasks = `/api/projects/${second.id}/tasks`;
    const createTask = (path, title) => fetch(server.url + path, {
      method: 'POST',
      headers: { 'Content-Type': 'application/json' },
      body: JSON.stringify({ title }),
    });
    const completeTask = (path, completed) => fetch(server.url + path, {
      method: 'PATCH',
      headers: { 'Content-Type': 'application/json' },
      body: JSON.stringify({ completed }),
    });
    assert.deepEqual(await get(firstTasks), []);
    for (const title of ['', ' \t\n ']) {
      const response = await createTask(firstTasks, title);
      assert.equal(response.status, 400);
      assert.deepEqual(await response.json(), { error: 'Task title is required' });
    }
    assert.deepEqual(await get(firstTasks), []);
    const taskResponse = await createTask(firstTasks, '  First task  ');
    assert.equal(taskResponse.status, 201);
    const firstTask = await taskResponse.json();
    assert.ok(firstTask.id);
    assert.equal(firstTask.title, 'First task');
    assert.equal(firstTask.completed, false);
    assert.equal(firstTask.priority, 'Normal');
    const nextTaskResponse = await createTask(firstTasks, 'Second task');
    const secondTask = await nextTaskResponse.json();
    assert.notEqual(firstTask.id, secondTask.id);
    assert.deepEqual(await get(firstTasks), [firstTask, secondTask]);
    assert.deepEqual(await get(secondTasks), []);
    const otherTaskResponse = await createTask(secondTasks, 'Other project task');
    const otherTask = await otherTaskResponse.json();
    assert.equal(secondTask.priority, 'Normal');
    assert.equal(otherTask.priority, 'Normal');
    assert.deepEqual(await get(secondTasks), [otherTask]);
    const wrongProject = await completeTask(`${secondTasks}/${firstTask.id}`, true);
    assert.equal(wrongProject.status, 404);
    const invalidCompletion = await completeTask(`${firstTasks}/${firstTask.id}`, 'true');
    assert.equal(invalidCompletion.status, 400);
    assert.deepEqual(await get(firstTasks), [firstTask, secondTask]);
    const completion = await completeTask(`${firstTasks}/${firstTask.id}`, true);
    assert.equal(completion.status, 200);
    firstTask.completed = true;
    assert.deepEqual(await completion.json(), firstTask);
    const reopened = await completeTask(`${firstTasks}/${firstTask.id}`, false);
    assert.equal(reopened.status, 200);
    firstTask.completed = false;
    assert.deepEqual(await reopened.json(), firstTask);
    await completeTask(`${firstTasks}/${firstTask.id}`, true);
    firstTask.completed = true;
    assert.deepEqual(await get(firstTasks), [firstTask, secondTask]);
    assert.deepEqual(await get(secondTasks), [otherTask]);
    const unknownProject = await createTask('/api/projects/missing/tasks', 'Orphan');
    assert.equal(unknownProject.status, 404);
    first.total = 2;
    first.completed = 1;
    second.total = 1;
    const setPriority = (path, priority) => fetch(server.url + path, {
      method: 'PATCH',
      headers: { 'Content-Type': 'application/json' },
      body: JSON.stringify({ priority }),
    });
    assert.equal((await setPriority(`${secondTasks}/${firstTask.id}`, 'High')).status, 404);
    for (const priority of ['', 'high', 'Urgent', null, 123]) {
      assert.equal((await setPriority(`${firstTasks}/${firstTask.id}`, priority)).status, 400);
      assert.deepEqual(await get(firstTasks), [firstTask, secondTask]);
    }
    for (const priority of ['Low', 'Normal', 'High']) {
      const response = await setPriority(`${firstTasks}/${firstTask.id}`, priority);
      assert.equal(response.status, 200);
      firstTask.priority = priority;
      assert.deepEqual(await response.json(), firstTask);
      assert.deepEqual(await get(firstTasks), [firstTask, secondTask]);
      assert.deepEqual(await get(secondTasks), [otherTask]);
      assert.deepEqual(await get('/api/projects'), [existing, first, second]);
    }
    assert.equal((await setPriority(`${firstTasks}/${secondTask.id}`, 'Low')).status, 200);
    secondTask.priority = 'Low';
    const renameTask = (path, title) => fetch(server.url + path, {
      method: 'PATCH',
      headers: { 'Content-Type': 'application/json' },
      body: JSON.stringify({ title }),
    });
    assert.equal((await renameTask(`${secondTasks}/${firstTask.id}`, 'Wrong owner')).status, 404);
    for (const title of ['', ' \t\n ', null, 123]) {
      const response = await renameTask(`${firstTasks}/${firstTask.id}`, title);
      assert.equal(response.status, 400);
      assert.deepEqual(await response.json(), { error: 'Task title is required' });
      assert.deepEqual(await get(firstTasks), [firstTask, secondTask]);
    }
    const renamedTask = await renameTask(`${firstTasks}/${firstTask.id}`, '  Renamed completed task  ');
    assert.equal(renamedTask.status, 200);
    firstTask.title = 'Renamed completed task';
    assert.deepEqual(await renamedTask.json(), firstTask);
    const renamedOpenTask = await renameTask(`${firstTasks}/${secondTask.id}`, '  Renamed open task  ');
    assert.equal(renamedOpenTask.status, 200);
    secondTask.title = 'Renamed open task';
    assert.deepEqual(await renamedOpenTask.json(), secondTask);
    assert.deepEqual(await get(firstTasks), [firstTask, secondTask]);
    assert.deepEqual(await get(secondTasks), [otherTask]);
    assert.deepEqual(await get('/api/projects'), [existing, first, second]);
    const rename = name => fetch(server.url + `/api/projects/${first.id}`, {
      method: 'PATCH',
      headers: { 'Content-Type': 'application/json' },
      body: JSON.stringify({ name }),
    });
    for (const name of ['', ' \t\n ', null, 123]) {
      const response = await rename(name);
      assert.equal(response.status, 400);
      assert.deepEqual(await response.json(), { error: 'Project name is required' });
      assert.deepEqual(await get(`/api/projects/${first.id}`), first);
    }
    const renamed = await rename('  Renamed project  ');
    assert.equal(renamed.status, 200);
    first.name = 'Renamed project';
    assert.deepEqual(await renamed.json(), first);
    assert.deepEqual(await get('/api/projects'), [existing, first, second]);
    assert.deepEqual(await get(firstTasks), [firstTask, secondTask]);
    const setArchived = archived => fetch(server.url + `/api/projects/${first.id}`, {
      method: 'PATCH',
      headers: { 'Content-Type': 'application/json' },
      body: JSON.stringify({ archived }),
    });
    assert.equal((await setArchived('true')).status, 400);
    const archiveResponse = await setArchived(true);
    assert.equal(archiveResponse.status, 200);
    first.archived = true;
    assert.deepEqual(await archiveResponse.json(), first);
    assert.deepEqual(await get('/api/projects'), [existing, first, second]);
    assert.equal((await createTask(firstTasks, 'Blocked')).status, 409);
    assert.equal((await completeTask(`${firstTasks}/${firstTask.id}`, false)).status, 409);
    assert.equal((await renameTask(`${firstTasks}/${firstTask.id}`, 'Blocked task rename')).status, 409);
    assert.equal((await setPriority(`${firstTasks}/${firstTask.id}`, 'Low')).status, 409);
    assert.equal((await rename('Blocked rename')).status, 409);
    assert.deepEqual(await get(`/api/projects/${first.id}`), first);
    assert.deepEqual(await get(firstTasks), [firstTask, secondTask]);
    for (const path of ['/', `/projects/${first.id}`]) {
      const response = await fetch(server.url + path);
      assert.equal(response.status, 200);
      const page = await response.text();
      assert.match(page, /<h1>Workboard<\/h1>/);
      assert.match(page, /<label for="project-name">Project name<\/label>/);
      assert.match(page, /Create project/);
      assert.match(page, /role="alert"/);
      assert.match(page, /<label for="new-project-name">New project name<\/label>/);
      assert.match(page, /Rename project/);
    }
    await server.stop();
    server = undefined;
    server = await start(databasePath);
    assert.deepEqual(await get('/api/projects/legacy/tasks'), legacyTasks);
    assert.deepEqual(await get('/api/projects'), [existing, first, second]);
    assert.deepEqual(await get(`/api/projects/${first.id}`), first);
    assert.deepEqual(await get(firstTasks), [firstTask, secondTask]);
    assert.deepEqual(await get(secondTasks), [otherTask]);
    assert.equal((await createTask(firstTasks, 'Still blocked')).status, 409);
    assert.equal((await renameTask(`${firstTasks}/${firstTask.id}`, 'Still blocked rename')).status, 409);
    assert.equal((await setPriority(`${firstTasks}/${firstTask.id}`, 'Normal')).status, 409);
    const restored = await setArchived(false);
    first.archived = false;
    assert.equal(restored.status, 200);
    assert.deepEqual(await restored.json(), first);
    assert.equal((await setPriority(`${firstTasks}/${firstTask.id}`, 'Low')).status, 200);
    firstTask.priority = 'Low';
    const renamedAfterRestoration = await rename('  Restored and renamed  ');
    assert.equal(renamedAfterRestoration.status, 200);
    first.name = 'Restored and renamed';
    assert.deepEqual(await renamedAfterRestoration.json(), first);
    const taskRenamedAfterRestoration = await renameTask(`${firstTasks}/${firstTask.id}`, '  Restored task  ');
    assert.equal(taskRenamedAfterRestoration.status, 200);
    firstTask.title = 'Restored task';
    assert.deepEqual(await taskRenamedAfterRestoration.json(), firstTask);
    const reopenedAfterRestart = await completeTask(`${firstTasks}/${firstTask.id}`, false);
    assert.equal(reopenedAfterRestart.status, 200);
    firstTask.completed = false;
    assert.deepEqual(await get(firstTasks), [firstTask, secondTask]);
    first.completed = 0;
    assert.deepEqual(await get('/api/projects'), [existing, first, second]);
    await server.stop();
    server = undefined;
    server = await start(databasePath);
    assert.deepEqual(await get('/api/projects'), [existing, first, second]);
    assert.deepEqual(await get(firstTasks), [firstTask, secondTask]);
  } finally {
    if (server) await server.stop();
    await rm(directory, { recursive: true, force: true });
  }
});

test('project defaults affect only future tasks and persist through rename, archive, restore, and restart', async () => {
  await mkdir('data', { recursive: true });
  const directory = await mkdtemp(resolve('data', 'defaults-test-'));
  let server;
  try {
    const databasePath = resolve(directory, 'defaults.sqlite');
    server = await start(databasePath);
    const api = async (path, method = 'GET', body, status = 200) => {
      const response = await fetch(server.url + path, {
        method,
        ...(body === undefined ? {} : {
          headers: { 'Content-Type': 'application/json' }, body: JSON.stringify(body),
        }),
      });
      assert.equal(response.status, status);
      return response.json();
    };
    const first = await api('/api/projects', 'POST', { name: 'First' }, 201);
    const second = await api('/api/projects', 'POST', { name: 'Second' }, 201);
    const path = `/api/projects/${first.id}`;
    const otherPath = `/api/projects/${second.id}`;
    assert.equal(first.default_task_priority, 'Normal');
    assert.equal(second.default_task_priority, 'Normal');
    const original = await api(`${path}/tasks`, 'POST', { title: 'Original' }, 201);
    assert.equal(original.priority, 'Normal');
    for (const invalid of ['', 'high', 'Urgent', null, 123]) {
      await api(path, 'PATCH', { default_task_priority: invalid }, 400);
      assert.equal((await api(path)).default_task_priority, 'Normal');
    }
    await api(path, 'PATCH', { default_task_priority: 'High' });
    const inherited = await api(`${path}/tasks`, 'POST', { title: 'Inherited' }, 201);
    assert.equal(inherited.priority, 'High');
    await api(`${path}/tasks/${inherited.id}`, 'PATCH', { completed: true });
    inherited.completed = true;
    await api(`${path}/tasks/${inherited.id}`, 'PATCH', { title: 'Renamed task' });
    inherited.title = 'Renamed task';
    const unchanged = [original, inherited];
    await api(path, 'PATCH', { default_task_priority: 'Low' });
    assert.deepEqual(await api(`${path}/tasks`), unchanged);
    assert.equal((await api(otherPath)).default_task_priority, 'Normal');
    const otherTask = await api(`${otherPath}/tasks`, 'POST', { title: 'Other' }, 201);
    assert.equal(otherTask.priority, 'Normal');
    await api(otherPath, 'PATCH', { default_task_priority: 'High' });
    await api(path, 'PATCH', { name: 'Renamed project' });
    const renamed = await api(path);
    assert.equal(renamed.default_task_priority, 'Low');
    assert.equal(renamed.completed, 1);
    assert.equal(renamed.total, 2);
    await api(path, 'PATCH', { archived: true });
    await api(path, 'PATCH', { default_task_priority: 'Normal' }, 409);
    await server.stop();
    server = await start(databasePath);
    assert.deepEqual(await api(path), { ...renamed, archived: true });
    assert.deepEqual(await api(`${path}/tasks`), unchanged);
    assert.equal((await api(otherPath)).default_task_priority, 'High');
    await api(path, 'PATCH', { archived: false });
    const lowTask = await api(`${path}/tasks`, 'POST', { title: 'After restoration' }, 201);
    assert.equal(lowTask.priority, 'Low');
    await api(path, 'PATCH', { default_task_priority: 'Normal' });
    assert.deepEqual(await api(`${path}/tasks`), [...unchanged, lowTask]);
    assert.deepEqual(await api(`${otherPath}/tasks`), [otherTask]);
    await server.stop();
    server = await start(databasePath);
    assert.equal((await api(path)).default_task_priority, 'Normal');
    assert.deepEqual(await api(`${path}/tasks`), [...unchanged, lowTask]);
    assert.deepEqual((await api('/api/projects')).map(project => project.id), [first.id, second.id]);
  } finally {
    if (server) await server.stop();
    await rm(directory, { recursive: true, force: true });
  }
});

test('due dates validate calendar days and persist independently through edits, archive, and restart', async () => {
  await mkdir('data', { recursive: true });
  const directory = await mkdtemp(resolve('data', 'dates-test-'));
  let server;
  try {
    const databasePath = resolve(directory, 'dates.sqlite');
    server = await start(databasePath);
    const api = async (path, method = 'GET', body, status = 200) => {
      const response = await fetch(server.url + path, {
        method,
        ...(body === undefined ? {} : {
          headers: { 'Content-Type': 'application/json' }, body: JSON.stringify(body),
        }),
      });
      assert.equal(response.status, status);
      return response.json();
    };
    const project = await api('/api/projects', 'POST', { name: 'Dates' }, 201);
    const other = await api('/api/projects', 'POST', { name: 'Other' }, 201);
    const path = `/api/projects/${project.id}`;
    const task = await api(`${path}/tasks`, 'POST', { title: 'First' }, 201);
    const second = await api(`${path}/tasks`, 'POST', { title: 'Second' }, 201);
    const taskPath = `${path}/tasks/${task.id}`;
    assert.equal(task.due_date, '');
    assert.equal(second.due_date, '');
    await api(taskPath, 'PATCH', { completed: true });
    task.completed = true;
    await api(taskPath, 'PATCH', { priority: 'High' });
    task.priority = 'High';
    const summary = await api(path);
    for (const date of ['0001-01-01', '0004-02-29', '2000-02-29', '2024-02-29', '9999-12-31']) {
      const saved = await api(taskPath, 'PATCH', { due_date: `  ${date} \t` });
      task.due_date = date;
      assert.deepEqual(saved, task);
      assert.deepEqual(await api(`${path}/tasks`), [task, second]);
      assert.deepEqual(await api(path), summary);
    }
    for (const date of ['0000-01-01', '10000-01-01', '1900-02-29', '2100-02-29',
      '2023-02-29', '2024-04-31', '2024-00-01', '2024-13-01', '2024-01-00',
      '2024-01-32', '2024-1-01', '24-01-01', '2024-01-01T00:00:00Z', 'invalid', null, 20240101]) {
      assert.deepEqual(await api(taskPath, 'PATCH', { due_date: date }, 400), {
        error: 'Due date must be a valid YYYY-MM-DD date',
      });
      assert.deepEqual(await api(`${path}/tasks`), [task, second]);
      assert.deepEqual(await api(path), summary);
    }
    await api(`/api/projects/${other.id}/tasks/${task.id}`, 'PATCH', { due_date: '2024-01-01' }, 404);
    await api(taskPath, 'PATCH', { title: 'Renamed' });
    task.title = 'Renamed';
    assert.deepEqual(await api(`${path}/tasks`), [task, second]);
    await api(path, 'PATCH', { archived: true });
    await api(taskPath, 'PATCH', { due_date: '' }, 409);
    await server.stop();
    server = await start(databasePath);
    assert.deepEqual(await api(`${path}/tasks`), [task, second]);
    await api(taskPath, 'PATCH', { due_date: '2025-01-01' }, 409);
    await api(path, 'PATCH', { archived: false });
    assert.deepEqual(await api(path), summary);
    for (const date of ['', ' \t\n ']) {
      task.due_date = '';
      assert.deepEqual(await api(taskPath, 'PATCH', { due_date: date }), task);
      await server.stop();
      server = await start(databasePath);
      assert.deepEqual(await api(`${path}/tasks`), [task, second]);
    }
    await api(`${path}/tasks/${second.id}`, 'PATCH', { due_date: '2026-10-11' });
    second.due_date = '2026-10-11';
    assert.deepEqual(await api(`${path}/tasks`), [task, second]);
    assert.deepEqual(await api(path), summary);
  } finally {
    if (server) await server.stop();
    await rm(directory, { recursive: true, force: true });
  }
});
import { test } from 'node:test';
import assert from 'node:assert/strict';
import { readFile } from 'node:fs/promises';
import { runInNewContext } from 'node:vm';

// Inline the shared module when running browser code in the dependency-free DOM harness.
async function appSource() {
  const [dates, app] = await Promise.all([
    readFile(new URL('../public/dates.js', import.meta.url), 'utf8'),
    readFile(new URL('../public/app.js', import.meta.url), 'utf8'),
  ]);
  return dates.replace('export function', 'function') + app.replace(/^import .*;\n/, '');
}

// Only the DOM operations used by the app are needed for these interaction checks.
class Element {
  children = [];
  dataset = {};
  attributes = {};
  listeners = {};
  value = '';
  hidden = false;
  textContent = '';
  append(...children) { this.children.push(...children); }
  replaceChildren(...children) { this.children = children; }
  setAttribute(name, value) { this.attributes[name] = value; }
  addEventListener(name, listener) { this.listeners[name] = listener; }
  querySelector() { return this.button; }
  focus() {}
  async dispatch(name) { await this.listeners[name]({ preventDefault() {} }); }
}

test('project rename validates, updates the heading, preserves the URL and tasks, and reports save failures', async () => {
  const source = await appSource();
  const elements = new Map();
  const element = selector => {
    if (!elements.has(selector)) elements.set(selector, new Element());
    return elements.get(selector);
  };
  for (const form of ['#project-form', '#task-form', '#rename-form']) {
    element(form).button = new Element();
  }
  element('#task-filter').value = 'all';
  element('#priority-filter').value = 'all';
  const location = { pathname: '/projects/example' };
  const document = { querySelector: element, createElement: () => new Element() };
  const writes = [];
  let failNextWrite = false;
  await runInNewContext(source, {
    document,
    window: { location },
    fetch: async (path, options) => {
      if (!options) {
        const body = path.endsWith('/tasks')
          ? [{ id: 'task', title: 'Existing task', completed: true, priority: 'Normal' }]
          : { id: 'example', name: 'Original', archived: false };
        return { ok: true, json: async () => body };
      }
      writes.push({ path, ...options });
      if (failNextWrite) return { ok: false, json: async () => ({ error: 'Save failed' }) };
      return { ok: true, json: async () => ({ id: 'example', name: JSON.parse(options.body).name }) };
    },
  });
  assert.equal(element('#rename-form').hidden, false);
  assert.equal(element('#rename-form').button.disabled, false);
  assert.equal(element('#new-project-name').disabled, false);
  for (const name of ['', ' \t ']) {
    element('#new-project-name').value = name;
    await element('#rename-form').dispatch('submit');
    assert.equal(element('#rename-alert').textContent, 'Project name is required');
    assert.equal(element('#rename-alert').hidden, false);
    assert.equal(element('#project-heading').textContent, 'Original');
  }
  assert.equal(writes.length, 0);
  element('#new-project-name').value = '  Renamed project  ';
  await element('#rename-form').dispatch('submit');
  assert.equal(writes[0].path, '/api/projects/example');
  assert.equal(writes[0].method, 'PATCH');
  assert.deepEqual(JSON.parse(writes[0].body), { name: 'Renamed project' });
  assert.equal(element('#project-heading').textContent, 'Renamed project');
  assert.equal(document.title, 'Renamed project · Workboard');
  assert.equal(location.pathname, '/projects/example');
  assert.equal(location.href, undefined);
  assert.equal(element('#rename-alert').hidden, true);
  assert.equal(element('#task-list').children[0].children[1].textContent, 'Existing task');
  assert.equal(element('#task-list').children[0].children[0].checked, true);
  failNextWrite = true;
  element('#new-project-name').value = 'Unsaved';
  await element('#rename-form').dispatch('submit');
  assert.equal(element('#project-heading').textContent, 'Renamed project');
  assert.equal(element('#rename-alert').textContent, 'Save failed');
  assert.equal(element('#rename-form').button.disabled, false);
});

test('task UI validates titles, filters in creation order, and saves checkbox changes', async () => {
  const source = await appSource();
  const elements = new Map();
  const element = selector => {
    if (!elements.has(selector)) elements.set(selector, new Element());
    return elements.get(selector);
  };
  element('#project-form').button = new Element();
  element('#task-form').button = new Element();
  element('#rename-form').button = new Element();
  element('#task-filter').value = 'all';
  element('#priority-filter').value = 'all';
  const savedTasks = [
    { id: 'one', title: 'First task', completed: false, priority: 'Normal' },
    { id: 'two', title: 'Second task', completed: true, priority: 'High' },
    { id: 'three', title: 'Third task', completed: false, priority: 'Low' },
  ];
  const writes = [];
  let failNextWrite = false;
  await runInNewContext(source, {
    document: { querySelector: element, createElement: () => new Element() },
    window: { location: { pathname: '/projects/example' } },
    fetch: async (path, options) => {
      let body;
      if (!options) {
        body = path.endsWith('/tasks') ? structuredClone(savedTasks) : { id: 'example', name: 'Example' };
      } else {
        writes.push({ path, ...options });
        if (failNextWrite) {
          failNextWrite = false;
          return { ok: false, json: async () => ({ error: 'Save failed' }) };
        }
        const input = JSON.parse(options.body);
        if (options.method === 'POST') {
          body = { id: 'four', title: input.title, completed: false, priority: 'Normal' };
          savedTasks.push(body);
        } else {
          const task = savedTasks.find(task => path.endsWith(`/${task.id}`));
          Object.assign(task, input);
          body = { ...task };
        }
      }
      return { ok: true, json: async () => body };
    },
  });
  const rows = () => element('#task-list').children;
  const titles = () => rows().map(row => row.children[1].textContent);
  const filter = async value => {
    element('#task-filter').value = value;
    await element('#task-filter').dispatch('change');
  };
  assert.equal(element('#project-heading').textContent, 'Example');
  assert.equal(element('#task-controls').hidden, false);
  assert.deepEqual(titles(), ['First task', 'Second task', 'Third task']);
  assert.ok(rows().every(row => row.dataset.testid === 'task-row'));
  assert.equal(rows()[0].children[0].attributes['aria-label'], 'Complete First task');
  assert.equal(rows()[1].children[0].checked, true);
  assert.deepEqual(rows().map(row => row.children[3].value), ['Normal', 'High', 'Low']);
  for (const row of rows()) {
    const priority = row.children[3];
    assert.equal(priority.attributes['aria-label'], 'Task priority');
    assert.equal(priority.disabled, false);
    assert.deepEqual(priority.children.map(option => option.textContent), ['Low', 'Normal', 'High']);
  }
  const renameRow = rows()[1];
  const renameForm = renameRow.children[2];
  const [renameInput, renameButton] = renameForm.children;
  assert.equal(renameInput.attributes['aria-label'], 'New task title');
  assert.equal(renameButton.textContent, 'Rename task');
  assert.equal(renameInput.disabled, false);
  assert.equal(renameButton.disabled, false);
  for (const title of ['', ' \t ']) {
    renameInput.value = title;
    await renameForm.dispatch('submit');
    assert.equal(element('#task-alert').textContent, 'Task title is required');
    assert.equal(element('#task-alert').hidden, false);
    assert.equal(renameRow.children[1].textContent, 'Second task');
  }
  assert.equal(writes.length, 0);
  renameInput.value = '  Renamed task  ';
  await renameForm.dispatch('submit');
  assert.equal(writes[0].path, '/api/projects/example/tasks/two');
  assert.deepEqual(JSON.parse(writes[0].body), { title: 'Renamed task' });
  assert.equal(renameRow.children[1].textContent, 'Renamed task');
  assert.equal(renameRow.children[0].attributes['aria-label'], 'Complete Renamed task');
  assert.equal(renameRow.children[0].checked, true);
  assert.equal(renameRow.children[3].value, 'High');
  assert.deepEqual(titles(), ['First task', 'Renamed task', 'Third task']);
  failNextWrite = true;
  renameInput.value = 'Failed rename';
  await renameForm.dispatch('submit');
  assert.equal(renameRow.children[1].textContent, 'Renamed task');
  assert.equal(element('#task-alert').textContent, 'Save failed');
  assert.equal(renameInput.disabled, false);
  assert.equal(renameButton.disabled, false);
  element('#task-title').value = ' \t ';
  await element('#task-form').dispatch('submit');
  assert.equal(element('#task-alert').textContent, 'Task title is required');
  assert.equal(element('#task-alert').hidden, false);
  assert.equal(writes.length, 2);
  assert.equal(rows().length, 3);
  const priority = rows()[1].children[3];
  priority.value = 'Low';
  await priority.dispatch('change');
  assert.equal(writes.at(-1).path, '/api/projects/example/tasks/two');
  assert.deepEqual(JSON.parse(writes.at(-1).body), { priority: 'Low' });
  assert.equal(savedTasks[1].priority, 'Low');
  assert.equal(priority.value, 'Low');
  assert.equal(priority.disabled, false);
  assert.equal(renameRow.children[0].checked, true);
  assert.deepEqual(titles(), ['First task', 'Renamed task', 'Third task']);
  assert.equal(rows()[0].children[3].value, 'Normal');
  failNextWrite = true;
  priority.value = 'High';
  await priority.dispatch('change');
  assert.equal(priority.value, 'Low');
  assert.equal(priority.disabled, false);
  assert.equal(element('#task-alert').textContent, 'Save failed');
  await filter('open');
  assert.deepEqual(titles(), ['First task', 'Third task']);
  const firstCheckbox = rows()[0].children[0];
  firstCheckbox.checked = true;
  await firstCheckbox.dispatch('change');
  assert.equal(writes.at(-1).path, '/api/projects/example/tasks/one');
  assert.equal(savedTasks[0].completed, true);
  assert.deepEqual(titles(), ['Third task']);
  await filter('completed');
  assert.deepEqual(titles(), ['First task', 'Renamed task']);
  const completedCheckbox = rows()[0].children[0];
  completedCheckbox.checked = false;
  await completedCheckbox.dispatch('change');
  assert.equal(savedTasks[0].completed, false);
  assert.deepEqual(titles(), ['Renamed task']);
  assert.equal(rows()[0].children[3].value, 'Low');
  element('#task-title').value = '  Fourth task  ';
  await element('#task-form').dispatch('submit');
  assert.equal(savedTasks[3].title, 'Fourth task');
  assert.equal(savedTasks[3].completed, false);
  assert.deepEqual(titles(), ['Renamed task']);
  await filter('all');
  assert.deepEqual(titles(), ['First task', 'Renamed task', 'Third task', 'Fourth task']);
  assert.equal(rows()[3].children[3].value, 'Normal');
  failNextWrite = true;
  const checkbox = rows()[0].children[0];
  checkbox.checked = true;
  await checkbox.dispatch('change');
  assert.equal(checkbox.checked, false);
  assert.equal(checkbox.disabled, false);
  assert.equal(element('#task-alert').textContent, 'Save failed');
});

test('project UI filters, summarizes, archives, and restores rows in creation order', async () => {
  const source = await appSource();
  const elements = new Map();
  const element = selector => {
    if (!elements.has(selector)) elements.set(selector, new Element());
    return elements.get(selector);
  };
  element('#project-form').button = new Element();
  element('#task-form').button = new Element();
  element('#rename-form').button = new Element();
  element('#project-filter').value = 'active';
  const projects = [
    { id: 'one', name: 'First', archived: false, completed: 1, total: 2 },
    { id: 'two', name: 'Second', archived: false, completed: 0, total: 0 },
  ];
  const location = { pathname: '/' };
  await runInNewContext(source, {
    document: { querySelector: element, createElement: () => new Element() },
    window: { location },
    fetch: async (path, options) => {
      if (!options) return { ok: true, json: async () => structuredClone(projects) };
      const project = projects.find(project => path.endsWith(`/${project.id}`));
      project.archived = JSON.parse(options.body).archived;
      return { ok: true, json: async () => ({ ...project }) };
    },
  });
  const rows = () => element('#project-list').children;
  assert.deepEqual(rows().map(row => row.children[0].textContent), ['First', 'Second']);
  assert.equal(rows()[0].dataset.testid, 'project-row');
  assert.equal(rows()[0].children[1].dataset.testid, 'project-summary');
  assert.equal(rows()[0].children[1].textContent, '1/2 completed');
  assert.equal(rows()[1].children[1].textContent, '0/0 completed');
  assert.equal(rows()[0].children[3].textContent, 'Archive project');
  await rows()[0].children[3].dispatch('click');
  assert.deepEqual(rows().map(row => row.children[0].textContent), ['Second']);
  element('#project-filter').value = 'archived';
  await element('#project-filter').dispatch('change');
  assert.equal(rows().length, 1);
  assert.equal(rows()[0].children[1].textContent, '1/2 completed');
  assert.equal(rows()[0].children[2].textContent, 'Open project');
  await rows()[0].children[2].dispatch('click');
  assert.equal(location.href, '/projects/one');
  assert.equal(rows()[0].children[3].textContent, 'Restore project');
  await rows()[0].children[3].dispatch('click');
  assert.equal(rows().length, 0);
  element('#project-filter').value = 'active';
  await element('#project-filter').dispatch('change');
  assert.deepEqual(rows().map(row => row.children[0].textContent), ['First', 'Second']);
});

test('archived project UI disables task changes while keeping filters usable', async () => {
  const source = await appSource();
  const elements = new Map();
  const element = selector => {
    if (!elements.has(selector)) elements.set(selector, new Element());
    return elements.get(selector);
  };
  element('#project-form').button = new Element();
  element('#task-form').button = new Element();
  element('#rename-form').button = new Element();
  element('#task-filter').value = 'all';
  element('#priority-filter').value = 'all';
  let writes = 0;
  await runInNewContext(source, {
    document: { querySelector: element, createElement: () => new Element() },
    window: { location: { pathname: '/projects/one' } },
    fetch: async (path, options) => {
      if (options) writes++;
      const body = path.endsWith('/tasks') ? [
        { id: 'a', title: 'Open task', completed: false, priority: 'Low' },
        { id: 'b', title: 'Done task', completed: true, priority: 'High' },
      ] : { id: 'one', name: 'Archived example', archived: true };
      return { ok: true, json: async () => body };
    },
  });
  const rows = () => element('#task-list').children;
  assert.equal(element('#archived-message').hidden, false);
  assert.equal(element('#task-form').button.disabled, true);
  assert.equal(element('#rename-form').hidden, false);
  assert.equal(element('#rename-form').button.disabled, true);
  assert.equal(element('#new-project-name').disabled, true);
  element('#new-project-name').value = 'Blocked rename';
  await element('#rename-form').dispatch('submit');
  assert.equal(rows().length, 2);
  assert.ok(rows().every(row => row.children[0].disabled));
  assert.ok(rows().every(row => row.children[3].disabled));
  assert.deepEqual(rows().map(row => row.children[3].value), ['Low', 'High']);
  await rows()[0].children[3].dispatch('change');
  assert.ok(rows().every(row => row.children[2].children.every(control => control.disabled)));
  rows()[0].children[2].children[0].value = 'Blocked task rename';
  await rows()[0].children[2].dispatch('submit');
  element('#task-filter').value = 'completed';
  await element('#task-filter').dispatch('change');
  assert.equal(rows().length, 1);
  assert.equal(rows()[0].children[1].textContent, 'Done task');
  assert.equal(rows()[0].children[0].disabled, true);
  assert.equal(rows()[0].children[3].disabled, true);
  assert.equal(rows()[0].children[3].value, 'High');
  element('#task-filter').value = 'open';
  await element('#task-filter').dispatch('change');
  assert.equal(rows()[0].children[1].textContent, 'Open task');
  element('#task-title').value = 'Attempt';
  await element('#task-form').dispatch('submit');
  assert.equal(writes, 0);
});

test('combined filters retain selections and creation order across task edits and page loads', async () => {
  const source = await appSource();
  const savedTasks = [
    { id: 'a', title: 'Open low', completed: false, priority: 'Low' },
    { id: 'b', title: 'Done normal', completed: true, priority: 'Normal' },
    { id: 'c', title: 'Open high', completed: false, priority: 'High' },
    { id: 'd', title: 'Done low', completed: true, priority: 'Low' },
    { id: 'e', title: 'Open normal', completed: false, priority: 'Normal' },
    { id: 'f', title: 'Done high', completed: true, priority: 'High' },
  ];
  let writes = 0;
  const loadPage = async archived => {
    const elements = new Map();
    const element = selector => {
      if (!elements.has(selector)) elements.set(selector, new Element());
      return elements.get(selector);
    };
    for (const form of ['#project-form', '#task-form', '#rename-form']) {
      element(form).button = new Element();
    }
    element('#task-filter').value = 'all';
    element('#priority-filter').value = 'all';
    await runInNewContext(source, {
      document: { querySelector: element, createElement: () => new Element() },
      window: { location: { pathname: '/projects/example' } },
      fetch: async (path, options) => {
        if (!options) {
          const body = path.endsWith('/tasks') ? structuredClone(savedTasks)
            : { id: 'example', name: 'Example', archived };
          return { ok: true, json: async () => body };
        }
        writes++;
        assert.equal(archived, false);
        const task = savedTasks.find(task => path.endsWith(`/${task.id}`));
        Object.assign(task, JSON.parse(options.body));
        return { ok: true, json: async () => ({ ...task }) };
      },
    });
    return {
      element,
      rows: () => element('#task-list').children,
      titles: () => element('#task-list').children.map(row => row.children[1].textContent),
      async filter(selector, value) {
        element(selector).value = value;
        await element(selector).dispatch('change');
      },
    };
  };
  const page = await loadPage(false);
  for (const completion of ['all', 'open', 'completed']) {
    await page.filter('#task-filter', completion);
    for (const priority of ['all', 'Low', 'Normal', 'High']) {
      await page.filter('#priority-filter', priority);
      assert.equal(page.element('#task-filter').value, completion);
      assert.deepEqual(page.titles(), savedTasks.filter(task =>
        (completion === 'all' || task.completed === (completion === 'completed')) &&
        (priority === 'all' || task.priority === priority)
      ).map(task => task.title));
    }
  }
  assert.equal(writes, 0);
  await page.filter('#task-filter', 'open');
  assert.equal(page.element('#priority-filter').value, 'High');
  const rename = page.rows()[0].children[2];
  rename.children[0].value = '  Renamed high  ';
  await rename.dispatch('submit');
  assert.deepEqual(page.titles(), ['Renamed high']);
  assert.equal(page.rows()[0].children[0].attributes['aria-label'], 'Complete Renamed high');
  assert.equal(page.rows()[0].children[3].value, 'High');
  const priority = page.rows()[0].children[3];
  priority.value = 'Low';
  await priority.dispatch('change');
  assert.deepEqual(page.titles(), []);
  assert.equal(page.element('#task-filter').value, 'open');
  assert.equal(page.element('#priority-filter').value, 'High');
  await page.filter('#priority-filter', 'Low');
  assert.deepEqual(page.titles(), ['Open low', 'Renamed high']);
  const checkbox = page.rows()[0].children[0];
  checkbox.checked = true;
  await checkbox.dispatch('change');
  assert.deepEqual(page.titles(), ['Renamed high']);
  assert.equal(page.element('#task-filter').value, 'open');
  assert.equal(page.element('#priority-filter').value, 'Low');
  await page.filter('#task-filter', 'completed');
  assert.deepEqual(page.titles(), ['Open low', 'Done low']);
  const completedCheckbox = page.rows()[1].children[0];
  completedCheckbox.checked = false;
  await completedCheckbox.dispatch('change');
  assert.deepEqual(page.titles(), ['Open low']);
  assert.equal(page.element('#task-filter').value, 'completed');
  assert.equal(page.element('#priority-filter').value, 'Low');
  assert.equal(writes, 4);

  const archivedPage = await loadPage(true);
  assert.equal(archivedPage.element('#priority-filter').value, 'all');
  assert.equal(archivedPage.rows().length, 6);
  await archivedPage.filter('#task-filter', 'open');
  await archivedPage.filter('#priority-filter', 'Low');
  assert.deepEqual(archivedPage.titles(), ['Renamed high', 'Done low']);
  for (const row of archivedPage.rows()) {
    assert.equal(row.children[0].disabled, true);
    assert.equal(row.children[3].disabled, true);
    assert.ok(row.children[2].children.every(control => control.disabled));
  }
  assert.equal(writes, 4);
  const restoredPage = await loadPage(false);
  assert.equal(restoredPage.element('#priority-filter').value, 'all');
  assert.equal(restoredPage.rows().length, 6);
  assert.equal(restoredPage.rows()[2].children[3].value, 'Low');
  assert.equal(restoredPage.rows()[2].children[3].disabled, false);
});

test('priority filter has an accessible label and exactly the required ordered options', async () => {
  const html = await readFile(new URL('../public/index.html', import.meta.url), 'utf8');
  assert.match(html, /<label for="priority-filter">Priority filter<\/label>/);
  const select = html.match(/<select id="priority-filter">([\s\S]*?)<\/select>/)[1];
  assert.deepEqual([...select.matchAll(/<option[^>]*>([^<]+)<\/option>/g)].map(match => match[1]),
    ['All', 'Low', 'Normal', 'High']);
  assert.match(select, /<option value="all" selected>All<\/option>/);
});

test('default priority saves without changing filters or existing rows and loads in archived and restored pages', async () => {
  const source = await appSource();
  const project = { id: 'example', name: 'Example', archived: false, default_task_priority: 'Normal' };
  const savedTasks = [
    { id: 'one', title: 'Original', completed: false, priority: 'Normal' },
  ];
  let failNextWrite = false;
  const writes = [];
  const loadPage = async () => {
    const elements = new Map();
    const element = selector => {
      if (!elements.has(selector)) elements.set(selector, new Element());
      return elements.get(selector);
    };
    for (const form of ['#project-form', '#task-form', '#rename-form']) {
      element(form).button = new Element();
    }
    element('#task-filter').value = 'all';
    element('#priority-filter').value = 'all';
    await runInNewContext(source, {
      document: { querySelector: element, createElement: () => new Element() },
      window: { location: { pathname: '/projects/example' } },
      fetch: async (path, options) => {
        let body;
        if (!options) body = path.endsWith('/tasks') ? savedTasks : project;
        else {
          writes.push({ path, ...options });
          if (failNextWrite) {
            failNextWrite = false;
            return { ok: false, json: async () => ({ error: 'Save failed' }) };
          }
          assert.equal(project.archived, false);
          const input = JSON.parse(options.body);
          if (options.method === 'POST') {
            body = { id: 'two', title: input.title, completed: false, priority: project.default_task_priority };
            savedTasks.push(body);
          } else {
            Object.assign(project, input);
            body = project;
          }
        }
        return { ok: true, json: async () => structuredClone(body) };
      },
    });
    return element;
  };
  const element = await loadPage();
  const defaultPriority = element('#default-task-priority');
  assert.equal(defaultPriority.value, 'Normal');
  assert.equal(defaultPriority.disabled, false);
  element('#task-filter').value = 'open';
  await element('#task-filter').dispatch('change');
  element('#priority-filter').value = 'Normal';
  await element('#priority-filter').dispatch('change');
  const originalRow = element('#task-list').children[0];
  defaultPriority.value = 'High';
  await defaultPriority.dispatch('change');
  assert.equal(writes[0].path, '/api/projects/example');
  assert.deepEqual(JSON.parse(writes[0].body), { default_task_priority: 'High' });
  assert.equal(defaultPriority.value, 'High');
  assert.equal(defaultPriority.disabled, false);
  assert.equal(element('#task-filter').value, 'open');
  assert.equal(element('#priority-filter').value, 'Normal');
  assert.equal(element('#task-list').children[0], originalRow);
  assert.equal(originalRow.children[3].value, 'Normal');
  element('#task-title').value = 'Inherited';
  await element('#task-form').dispatch('submit');
  assert.equal(savedTasks[1].priority, 'High');
  assert.equal(element('#task-list').children.length, 1);
  assert.equal(element('#priority-filter').value, 'Normal');
  failNextWrite = true;
  defaultPriority.value = 'Low';
  await defaultPriority.dispatch('change');
  assert.equal(defaultPriority.value, 'High');
